\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Bus vs.\ car passenger delay for each strategy. The green quadrant (both axes below dashed baseline lines) is the Pareto-improvement zone where both bus and car passengers benefit. Point size indicates grant rate; color indicates total passenger delay. WaveGate, NashGate, and CellSearch are the only strategies in the both-better zone. CPD-QL and CellQLearn sit in the both-worse quadrant (no balance guard, or a guard that has not yet converged).}}{32}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bus_car}{{2}{32}{Bus vs.\ car passenger delay for each strategy. The green quadrant (both axes below dashed baseline lines) is the Pareto-improvement zone where both bus and car passengers benefit. Point size indicates grant rate; color indicates total passenger delay. WaveGate, NashGate, and CellSearch are the only strategies in the both-better zone. CPD-QL and CellQLearn sit in the both-worse quadrant (no balance guard, or a guard that has not yet converged)}{figure.2}{}}
